From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:08:42 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] platform-pcecd

PC Engine CD-ROM2 and TurboGrafx-CD discs get their own shelf,
Games/PCECD, for .cue, .chd and .ccd, on the Beetle PCE Fast core the
TurboGrafx-16 already ships (Platform::Pcecd after Sgx; no new core).
Track files (.bin, .img, .sub) and playlists stay off the shelf, and a
disc on the TurboGrafx-16 shelf is skipped: that shelf stays .pce only.
It plays and draws like the TurboGrafx-16: B is II, A is I, START is
Run, SELECT after the chord hold, X and Y feed slot's turbo, L1 and R1
stay slot's picture keys, L2 and R2 rewind and fast-forward.

The Beetle PCE Fast list now also answers pce_fast_cdbios with "System
Card 3" (BIOS/syscard3.pce, the file the BIOS check will read) and
pce_fast_cdimagecache disabled (a disc is streamed, never loaded whole);
the CD speed, volume and filter keys stay at the core's defaults.

The Screen page gains a PC Engine CD section, last: Shader (the retro
list, Config/pcecd_shader.txt) and Picture, which starts at Crop (8 lines
off the top and bottom) and walks Stretch, Actual and 4:3, kept in
Config/picture.txt as pcecd. Saves are the 2 KB HUBM backup RAM in
Saves/PCECD. The release date for the shelf order is 4 December 1988,
between the Mega Drive and the Game Boy. Until the cart patch a disc
wears the US jewel case.
